# rrm_meta.config — sits next to rrm_meta.py.
#
# Files are now keyed by preset + PAIR + TIMEFRAME, so the EA on a EURUSD M1 chart
# writes/reads  TS_events_RRM_ORG_EURUSD_M1.csv  and  MetaModel_RRM_ORG_EURUSD_M1.csv .
#
# DURABILITY + FLOW (Ladder 2):
#   1) After EACH collect:   python3 rrm_meta.py --archive
#        -> pulls the fresh TS_events_* out of the wipe-prone tester agent sandbox
#           into the durable  MetaTrader 5/Files_SEA/events/  (merges + de-dupes by
#           event_time). Run it BEFORE the next collect, or that collect can be wiped.
#   2) To train:             python3 rrm_meta.py
#        -> archives anything new, then trains ONE model per pair+TF FROM Files_SEA/
#           events/, and writes each  MetaModel_<preset>_<PAIR>_<TF>.csv  into the
#           terminal  MQL5/Files/  (the folder the EA reads at GATE startup / live).
#        -> IDEMPOTENT: a pair+TF whose model is newer than its events file is skipped
#           ("up to date"), so re-running after a new pair only trains the new one.
#           --force retrains everything; --dry-run lists what it would do, writes nothing.
#
# files_dir can stay blank (auto-search). pair/tf below are only a fallback for a
# legacy unkeyed events file; per-pair files carry their own pair+TF in the name.
# To train just one pair:  python3 rrm_meta.py --pair EURUSD --tf M1

[meta]
files_dir =
pair   = GBPUSD
tf     = M15
preset = RRM_ORG
